<title>GERMANY: Mercedes says sees record output in 1996.</title>
<headline>Mercedes says sees record output in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>STUTTGART, Germany 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>German car-maker Mercedes-Benz AG on Tuesday said it would produce a record 630,000 cars in 1996, bringing its total output since World War Two to 15 million units.</p>
<p>In a statement, Mercedes also said work could begin in January on its new plant in Brazil, which is to produce A-class model cars, and production could start at the beginning of 1999.</p>
<p>The plant would have annual capacity of 70,000 vehicles.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
